    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17154,
        "title": "Nomes de Variáveis",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145108,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Bem-vindo ao <strong>JavaScript</strong>, uma linguagem de programação versátil para jogos.</p><p>Vamos analisar detalhadamente o JavaScript, uma <strong>linguagem</strong> de <strong>programação</strong> que pode controlar a lógica de jogos, animações e interações.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145109,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Os jogos precisam lembrar de coisas como a saúde do jogador, a pontuação e a posição. Para isso, o JavaScript tem <strong>variáveis</strong>.</p><p>Assim como os slots de itens, as variáveis armazenam valores e têm nomes que nos dizem o que elas contêm.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145110,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Usamos <code>const</code> para criar uma variável.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" myVariable\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"set\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145111,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Cada variável precisa de um <strong>nome</strong>. Os nomes das variáveis precisam ser palavras únicas e, portanto, não podem ter espaços.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"player score\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"9\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>score</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145112,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para criar nomes de variáveis com várias palavras, usamos o <strong>camel case</strong>. Começamos com uma letra minúscula e capitalizamos as palavras adicionais.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"player health\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"16\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerHealth\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>playerHealth</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145113,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para nos ajudar a entender o que há dentro de uma variável, escolhemos nomes descritivos.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"eS\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"16\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemySpeed\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>enemySpeed</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145114,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que há de errado com este nome de variável?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player Health\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Contém um espaço</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Contém uma letra maiúscula</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Contém um espaço.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145115,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Por que damos nomes descritivos às variáveis como <code>playerHealth</code> ou <code>score</code> em vez de <code>x</code> ou <code>y</code>?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Para nos ajudar a entender o que há dentro deles</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Para torná-los mais rápidos de digitar</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Para nos ajudar a entender o que há dentro deles.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145116,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quais palavras podemos usar para declarar variáveis?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>let</code> e <code>const</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>let</code> e <code>variable</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>let</code> e <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145117,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para que usamos camel case?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Para criar nomes de variáveis com várias palavras</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Para criar nomes de variáveis com espaços</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Para criar nomes de variáveis com várias palavras.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145118,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Escolha o nome de variável mais descritivo.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"phs\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"21\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerHighScore\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>playerHighScore</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145119,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Soletrar a palavra para uma das maneiras que usamos para criar uma variável.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"1\" endIndex=\"2\" /><option startIndex=\"2\" endIndex=\"3\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>l</code> seguido de <code>e</code> e finalmente <code>t</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145120,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Coloque os trechos na ordem correta para criar um nome de variável.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"15\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerScore\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>let</code> seguido de <code>playerScore</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 145121,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Conclua a criação desta variável codificando <code>let</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>let</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17155,
        "title": "Valores de Variáveis",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145122,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Os nomes de variáveis podem conter <strong>números</strong> também. Adicionar números é útil com várias variáveis semelhantes. Vamos criar a variável <code>enemy1</code> aqui.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"1 enemy\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"12\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy1\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>enemy1</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145123,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Depois de criar e nomear uma variável, usamos o sinal <code>=</code> para armazenar um <strong>valor</strong> dentro dela. Como <code>const levelName = \"Forest\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Forest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>=</code> seguido de <code>\"Forest\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145124,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para terminar de criar uma variável, colocamos um ponto e vírgula, <code>;</code>, no final da linha.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\".\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"27\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Forest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145125,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Os valores que temos armazenado como <code>\"Forest\"</code> são <strong>strings</strong>. Strings são palavras entre aspas duplas.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"&quot;Forest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>\"</code> seguido de <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145126,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Strings podem conter todos os tipos de letras e símbolos, incluindo espaços. Por exemplo, <code>\"Game Over\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"1\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"&quot;Game Over&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>\"</code> seguido de <code>Game Over</code> e finalmente <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145127,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Qual é o valor desta variável?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Karin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>\"Karin\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>playerName</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>\"Karin\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145128,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Como sabemos que um valor é uma string?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">É uma palavra entre aspas duplas</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">Contém um sinal <code>=</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">É uma palavra entre aspas duplas.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145129,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que está acontecendo neste código?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" gameState = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Playing&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A variável <code>gameState</code> armazena o valor <code>\"Playing\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A variável <code>\"Playing\"</code> armazena o valor <code>gameState</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A variável <code>gameState</code> armazena o valor <code>\"Playing\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145130,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Qual é o nome desta variável?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" weapon = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Tree shaping&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>weapon</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"Tree shaping\"</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>weapon</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145131,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Crie uma variável <code>playerClass</code> e atribua a ela o valor <code>\"Plumber\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"41\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"53\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mario&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerClass = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Plumber&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>let playerClass</code> seguido de <code>=</code> e finalmente <code>\"Plumber\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145132,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Crie uma variável <code>studio</code> e atribua a ela um valor de string.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Apple\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"21\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" studio = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>let studio</code> seguido de <code>=</code> e depois <code>\"Apple\"</code>, <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145133,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Atribua à variável <code>spawnPoint</code> um valor de string.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" spawnPoint = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Malta&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>\"</code> seguido de <code>Malta</code> e finalmente <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145134,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Atribua à variável <code>platform</code> o valor de string <code>\"Desktop\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"26\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" platform = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Desktop&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>\"Desktop\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17156,
        "title": "Diferenças entre Let e Const",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145135,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Já sabemos que podemos declarar variáveis com <code>let</code> e <code>const</code>. Vamos descobrir a diferença entre elas em um jogo!</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145136,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Usamos <code>const</code> para declarar valores que não devem mudar durante o jogo. <code>const</code> é a abreviação de \"constante\".</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" STARTING_LEVEL = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>const</code> seguido de <code>STARTING_LEVEL</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145137,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Se tentarmos atualizar um valor armazenado em uma variável <code>const</code>, receberemos um erro.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" MAX_HEALTH = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"MAX_HEALTH = \" /><text value=\"120\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145138,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>No entanto, podemos atualizar variáveis <code>let</code> com o operador de atribuição <code>=</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"const\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"score = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>let</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145139,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para deixar claro que uma variável é do tipo <code>const</code> e não deve mudar, podemos opcionalmente nomeá-la com letras maiúsculas.</p><p>Crie uma constante <code>spawn point</code> em maiúsculas.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"spawnPoint\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"spawn_point\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"17\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" SPAWN_POINT = \" /><text value=\"&quot;TownGate&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>SPAWN_POINT</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145140,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Não podemos usar <code>camelCase</code> se usarmos este padrão de letras maiúsculas, então usamos um <code>snake_case</code> em maiúsculas para nomear variáveis com mais de uma palavra.</p><p>Crie uma const \"player max health\" em <em>uppercase</em> usando <code>snake_case</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"player_max_health\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"playerMaxHealth\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"23\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" PLAYER_MAX_HEALTH = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>PLAYER_MAX_HEALTH</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145141,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Tanto <code>let</code> quanto <code>const</code> são formas úteis de declarar variáveis e poderíamos usá-las de forma intercambiável. No entanto, devemos tentar usar <code>const</code> como padrão.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"let\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" GAME_TITLE = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sprite Quest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145142,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>O que significa <code>const</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">constante</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">contínuo</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher constante.</p></body></html>"
